    "# AI401 - Experiment 5: Backward Chaining Engine with Askable Facts\n",
    "\n",
    "## Aim\n",
    "To implement a goal-driven backward-chaining engine for car-fault diagnosis using askable facts.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exercises covered\n",
    "1. Add a starter-motor fault based on clicking sound and an engine that does not crank.\n",
    "2. Change the hypothesis order and observe the questions asked.\n",
    "3. Provide a `WHY` option that explains the rule responsible for a question.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells in order. The demonstration cells use scripted answers so that the notebook runs without waiting for keyboard input. The final cell can be used interactively."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Knowledge base and backward-chaining engine\n",
    "\n",
    "A hypothesis is proved only when every condition in its rule is true. Askable conditions are obtained from the user; non-askable conditions can be proved recursively. Negative answers are remembered so that the same question is not asked again."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RULES = {\n",
    "    'battery_fault': ('dim_headlights', 'engine_not_cranking'),\n",
    "    'starter_motor_fault': ('clicking_sound', 'engine_not_cranking'),\n",
    "    'fuel_system_fault': ('engine_cranks', 'engine_does_not_start'),\n",
    "    'alternator_fault': ('battery_warning_light', 'battery_discharges'),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "QUESTIONS = {\n",
    "    'dim_headlights': 'Are the headlights dim?',\n",
    "    'engine_not_cranking': 'Is the engine not cranking?',\n",
    "    'clicking_sound': 'Do you hear a clicking sound when starting?',\n",
    "    'engine_cranks': 'Does the engine crank?',\n",
    "    'engine_does_not_start': 'Does the engine fail to start?',\n",
    "    'battery_warning_light': 'Is the battery warning light ON?',\n",
    "    'battery_discharges': 'Does the battery discharge quickly?',\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "DEFAULT_ORDER = ['battery_fault', 'starter_motor_fault',\n",
    "                 'fuel_system_fault', 'alternator_fault']\n",
    "\n",
    "def readable(name):\n",
    "    return name.replace('_', ' ').title()\n",
    "\n",
    "class BackwardChainingDiagnoser:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, answer_provider):\n",
    "        self.answer_provider = answer_provider\n",
    "        self.true_facts = set()\n",
    "        self.false_facts = set()\n",
    "        self.questions_asked = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    def explain_why(self, fact, goal):\n",
    "        conditions = ' AND '.join(RULES[goal])\n",
    "        return f\"WHY: checking {readable(goal)}. Rule: IF {conditions} THEN {goal}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def ask(self, fact, goal):\n",
    "        while True:\n",
    "            answer = self.answer_provider(fact, goal).strip().lower()\n",
    "            if answer == 'why':\n",
    "                print(self.explain_why(fact, goal))\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            if answer in {'yes', 'no'}:\n",
    "                self.questions_asked.append(fact)\n",
    "                (self.true_facts if answer == 'yes' else self.false_facts).add(fact)\n",
    "                return answer == 'yes'\n",
    "            print('Please enter yes, no, or WHY.')\n",
    "\n",
    "    def prove(self, goal):\n",
    "        if goal in self.true_facts:\n",
    "            return True\n",
    "        if goal in self.false_facts:\n",
    "            return False\n",
    "        if goal in QUESTIONS:\n",
    "            return self.ask(goal, goal)\n",
    "        if goal not in RULES:\n",
    "            return False\n",
    "        for condition in RULES[goal]:\n",
    "            if condition in QUESTIONS:\n",
    "                satisfied = self.ask(condition, goal) if condition not in self.true_facts | self.false_facts else condition in self.true_facts\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                satisfied = self.prove(condition)\n",
    "            if not satisfied:\n",
    "                return False\n",
    "        self.true_facts.add(goal)\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "\n",
    "    def diagnose(self, hypotheses=DEFAULT_ORDER):\n",
    "        for hypothesis in hypotheses:\n",
    "            print(f'Checking hypothesis: {readable(hypothesis)}')\n",
    "            if self.prove(hypothesis):\n",
    "                print(f'Diagnosis: {readable(hypothesis)}')\n",
    "                return hypothesis\n",
    "        print('Diagnosis: No fault could be diagnosed.')\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "def scripted_answers(*answers):\n",
    "    iterator = iter(answers)\n",
    "    def provider(fact, goal):\n",
    "        answer = next(iterator)\n",
    "        print(f'  {QUESTIONS[fact]} {answer}')\n",
    "        return answer\n",
    "    return provider\n"
   ]
  },
  {
